{"ref":"BDB, עַפְעַף","hw":"עַפְעַף","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">עַפְעַף</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 9:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.9.17\">Je 9:17</a> <strong>eyelid (</strong>NH id.<em>;</em> from <em>fluttering</em>?<strong>)</strong>;—only du. cstr. (v. infr.) and sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַפְעַפַּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 16:16\" href=\"/Job.16.16\">Jb 16:16</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 132:4\" href=\"/Psalms.132.4\">ψ 132:4</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עַפְעַפֶּיךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 4:25\" href=\"/Proverbs.4.25\">Pr 4:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:4\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.4\">6:4</a>, etc.;—<em>eyelids</em>, usually nearly = <em>eyes</em> (6 times ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">עֵינַיִם</span>), as weeping, <span dir=\"rtl\">עַפְעַפֵּינוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 9:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.9.17\">Je 9:17</a>; closed in sleep <a data-ref=\"Psalms 132:4\" href=\"/Psalms.132.4\">ψ 132:4</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:4\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.4\">Pr 6:4</a>, cf. of <a data-ref=\"BDB, צַלְמָוֶת\" href=\"/BDB,_צַלְמָוֶת\", dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמָוֶת</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 16:16\" href=\"/Job.16.16\">Jb 16:16</a>; looking <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 4:25\" href=\"/Proverbs.4.25\">Pr 4:25</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 11:4\" href=\"/Psalms.11.4\">ψ 11:4</a> (of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>, testing men); used seductively by wanton women <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:25\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.25\">Pr 6:25</a>; raised, in arrogance (‘<em>superciliousness</em>’) <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:13\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.13\">30:13</a>; fig. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַפְעַפֵּי־שָׁ֑חַר</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 3:9\" href=\"/Job.3.9\">Jb 3:9</a> <em>eyelids of dawn</em>, break of dawn, <a data-ref=\"Job 41:10\" href=\"/Job.41.10\">41:10</a> (sim.).","next":"BDB, עוּף²","prev":"BDB, עוֹף"}